<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">siege-master</ansi>

The Siege Master is the neutral elite of the Siegebreaker (Arbalist route;
no alignment asked). Its Piercing Bolt passes through its target and strikes
the foe behind it in the same column, a number of times a battle, and its
bolts tear armor away faster.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Ranks</ansi>

  30 Ballista bolt      once a battle, a Piercing Bolt passes through its
                        target and strikes the foe behind it in the column for
                        60% of the bolt's damage
  35 Sundering bolts II each bolt that lands takes 20 armor off the foe, up to
                        60
  40 Siege stock        a Piercing Bolt deals 50% more damage
  45 Ballista crew      the Ballista bolt works twice a battle
  50 Wall-breaker       each bolt that lands takes 25 armor off the foe, up to
                        75
  55 Heavy ballista     a Piercing Bolt deals 70% more damage, and the
                        Ballista bolt hits the foe behind for 80% of it
  60 Siege barrage      the Ballista bolt works four times a battle

It needs the Siegebreaker first (<ansi fg="command">help arbalist-routes</ansi>) and keeps every rank of it. At level 30 a
character that holds it promotes with <ansi fg="command">class promote [member] siege-master confirm</ansi>. Any alignment may take it.
Everything here lasts only for the battle and is never saved.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Elite talents</ansi>

Elite Arbalist talents (levels 35, 45, 55): Long Draw (+10% damage with a
shooting weapon), Eagle Eye (+5 Attack with a shooting weapon), Quick Nock
(starts a battle with 15 points on its action meter). See <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help arbalist-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help arbalist</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help elite</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help promotion</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.
